<title>SPAIN: Reuters seventh ex-Madrid air cargo market report.</title>
<headline>Reuters seventh ex-Madrid air cargo market report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below are the current average ex-Madrid Spanish peseta air cargo rates per kg for a 100 kg shipment with a volume-to-weight ratio of six-to-one.</p>
<p>			 Mar 6	  Jan 21</p>
<p>		   NORTH AMERICA</p>
<p> MAD-JFK	     190	    170</p>
<p> MAD-CHI	     200	    195</p>
<p> MAD-LAX	     200	    190</p>
<p> MAD-MIA	     235	    230</p>
<p>		   LATIN AMERICA</p>
<p> MAD-MEX	     315	    285</p>
<p> MAD-BAI	     450	    435</p>
<p> MAD-RIO	     445	    400</p>
<p>		   MIDDLE EAST</p>
<p> MAD-DXB	     240	    250</p>
<p>		   FAR EAST</p>
<p> MAD-HKG	     250	    240</p>
<p> MAD-TYO	     360	    360</p>
<p>These rates were obtained by Reuters journalists on a confidential basis from a range of airlines, general sales agents (GSAs) and freight forwarders. They exclude a current fuel surcharge. Cargo rates ex-Spain set to rise 5-10 percent by April.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
